  "raw_html": "<button type='button' role='link' class='btn btn-link p-0 text-start' id='link_10' aria-label=\" M/s. Nav Nirman Builders & Developers Pvt. Ltd. Through its Managing Director, Naveen Singh versus The Union of India Through Deputy Director, Directorate of Enforcement, Govt of India Ranchi, Jharkhand pdf\"  class='noToken' href='#' onclick=javascript:open_pdf('10','2026','2026_2_406_435','2026INSC130'); ><font size='4'> <strong>M/S. NAV NIRMAN BUILDERS & DEVELOPERS PVT. LTD. THROUGH ITS MANAGING DIRECTOR, NAVEEN SINGH<span class='fst-italic'> versus </span>THE UNION OF INDIA THROUGH DEPUTY DIRECTOR, DIRECTORATE OF ENFORCEMENT, GOVT OF INDIA RANCHI, JHARKHAND </strong>- <span class='escrText'>[2026] 2 S.C.R. 406</span><span class='ncDisplay'>2026 INSC 130</span><input type='hidden' id='cnr' value=ESCR010000492026></button></font><br><strong>Coram : M.M. SUNDRESH<sup style=\"color: #268e97;font-size: 22px;top: 0;\" class=\"tooltip-sup\" data-tooltip=\"Author\">*</sup>, N KOTISWAR SINGH</strong><br> Issue for Consideration In the instant case, this Court is concerned with the decision-making process adopted by the Special Court. Instead filed u/s.8(7) of the Prevention of Money-Laundering Act, 2002 (PMLA), and awaiting the adjudication by the Appellate Tribunal u/s.26 of the PMLA, the Special Court has allowed the said application. Headnotes&dagger; Prevention of Money-Laundering Act, 2002 &ndash; ss.8(7) and s.8(8):<br><strong class='caseDetailsTD' ><span style='color:#212F3D' > Decision Date :</span><font color='green'> 06-02-2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Case No :</span><font color='green'> CRIMINAL APPEAL No. 729/2026</font><span style='color:#212F3D' > | Disposal Nature :</span><font color='green'> Appeal(s) allowed</font>   <span style='color:#212F3D' > |  Bench :</span><font color='green'> 2 Judges</font></strong><div class='row my-1 mt-2 border bg-light'><div class='col-auto'><a href='#' class='btn btn-outline-secondary btn-sm my-1' on